      <div type="clause" n="6.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:LeisWl">Leis Wl</ref> 6.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="498–499" ed="#liebermann"/>E si aucuns vienged avant pur clamer la chose<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.2"/>, duinst gwage e truist plege, que, si auter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.1"/> le cleimt dedenz l’an e un jur, qu’il l’ait a dreit en la curt celui<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="ab" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.ab"/> ki l’avera truved.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-i"><pb n="498–499" ed="#liebermann"/>Si alquens vienge apref<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.6"/> pur clamer la jose<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="d" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.d"/>, dui[n]st<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="7" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.7"/> wage e troisse<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="8" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.8"/> pleges, que, si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.9"/> alter<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.10"/> claimid<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="e" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.e"/> l’aveir dedenz l’an e un jour, que<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.11"/> il l’ait a dreit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="12" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.12"/> en la curt celui qui l’averat troved.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" corresp="#wit-l"><pb n="498–499" ed="#liebermann"/>Quodsi quis uenerit rem ut suam clamans, det uadium et plegios, quod eam iudicio sistet<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="a" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.a"/>, si quis infra annum et diem eandem requisierit; et suum recipiat<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="b" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.b"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="xno" source="#robertson" n="6.1" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="256" ed="#robertson"/>E si aucuns vienged avant pur clamer la chose, duinst gwage e truist plege que, si auter le cleimt dedenz l'an e un jur, qu'il l'ait a dreit en la curt celui ki l'avera truved.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="498–499" ed="#liebermann"/>6, 1. Und wenn jemand hervortritt (herbeikommt<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.de.1"/> <hi rend="italic">I</hi>), um die Sache zu beanspruchen, so gebe [dieser Reclamant] Pfand und finde [dáfür] Bürgschaft (-gen <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>), dass, falls ein anderer binnen Jahr und Tag es beansprucht<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#LeisWl_6-1.lnote.de.2"/>, dass er es im [zuständigen] Gerichtshofe dessen, der es gefunden hat, zu Recht stellen werde.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">6, 1. And if someone steps forward (comes forward <hi rend="italic">I</hi>) to claim the thing, [this claimant] shall give pledge and find surety (-ies <hi rend="italic">IL</hi>) [for this], that, if another claims it within year and day, he will make it available at law in the [competent] court of him who has found it.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-hk"><pb n="257" ed="#robertson"/>And if anyone comes forward to claim the thing, he shall give pledge and find surety, that, if another claims it within a year and a day, he will bring it for decision to the court of the man who found it.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="499"><ref target="clause:LeisWl_5-2">Leis Wl 5.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">vgl. o. 5, 2</note>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 256–257 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text and German translation added from Gesetze I p. 498–499, October 2026 (two independent readings of the page images)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.ab" n="ab" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Genetiv KELHAM. SUCHIER</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">genitive KELHAM. SUCHIER</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">autre <hi rend="italic">ändert stets MAT.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">autre always emended by MAT.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">cose <hi rend="italic">ändert BA.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cose emended by BA.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.d" n="d" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl. Schuchardt</hi> Romania III 283</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. Schuchardt Romania III 283</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.e" n="e" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">clamud <hi rend="italic">Io; vgl. Foerster l. c.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">clamud Io; cf. Foerster l. c.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> 5, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. 5, 2</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.7" n="7" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">duist <hi rend="italic">Io;</hi> diust <hi rend="italic">Im</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">duist Io; diust Im</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.8" n="8" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">trosse <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">trosse Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">se <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">se Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">altre <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altre Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">qui <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">qui Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.12" n="12" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">498</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">droit <hi rend="italic">Io</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">droit Io</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.a" n="a" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">499</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Römische Phraseologie</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Roman phraseology</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.oe.b" n="b" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">499</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">erster Reclamant</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">first claimant</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">287</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">falsch <hi rend="italic">a prof</hi> (<hi rend="italic">proef</hi> Matzke) ‘zum Beweisen’ Frühere</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">wrongly <hi rend="italic">a prof</hi> (<hi rend="italic">proef</hi> Matzke) ‘for proving’ earlier editors</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="LeisWl_6-1.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">287</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Zur einjährigen Aufbewahrung des Fundes vergleicht schon Somner bei Wilkins den <hi rend="italic">Grand coutumier de Normandie</hi> c. 17. 19. Die Ausschlussfrist, innerhalb deren Eigentümer sein Recht beweise, ist auch anderwärts Jahr und Tag; J. Hübner 125. <hi rend="italic">S. o</hi>. 5, 2</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">On the keeping of the thing found for one year, Somner in Wilkins already compares the <hi rend="italic">Grand coutumier de Normandie</hi> c. 17. 19. The time limit within which the owner must prove his right is elsewhere too a year and a day; J. Hübner 125. <hi rend="italic">See above</hi> 5, 2</seg></note>
      </div>
